{
  "reason": "Use Tier 2: replace dot-product scoring with a learned-temperature cosine scoring head. Bidirectional masked reconstruction improved macro HR@10 to 0.5800, while the local convolution adapter reduced it to 0.5725, favoring an isolated change to scoring rather than additional context modules. Unconstrained embedding norms may distort rankings for sparse Amazon items; this is a testable hypothesis, not an established explanation for the plateau.",
  "module": [
    "model_design",
    "training_evaluation"
  ],
  "plan": {
    "data_processing_and_feature_engineering": null,
    "model_design": "Restore the reference MaskedSASRec without local_depthwise, local_projection, or local_gate, then make one experimental change: normalize query and candidate embeddings before their dot product and multiply by a jointly learned positive temperature scale. Implement a shared scoring helper using nn.functional.normalize with eps=1e-8 and exp(logit_scale).clamp(max=100), initializing logit_scale to log(10), while retaining the jointly trained item_bias. Use this identical head for positive logits, sampled-negative logits, and predict so training and inference optimize the same representation. Preserve MaskedSASRec constructor arguments, forward(self, sequence), predict(self, sequence, candidates), tied item_emb weights, bidirectional encoder, corruption strategy, and 256-negative sampled-softmax objective; train exactly one network per category.",
    "training_evaluation": "Update train_one and write_predict_script to reconstruct the cosine-head architecture, record its scoring specification in metadata, and strictly load one selected checkpoint per category. Preserve the reference optimizer, sampling, loss weighting, seed 42, supplied splits, epoch limit, patience, and fixed validation protocol so the scoring head is the only experimental factor relative to the 0.5800 reference. Verify shared-head training/prediction agreement, finite empty-history scores, and exported-predictor parity, then report actual selected-checkpoint macro HR@10 with Final Validation Score as the final log line; treat host evaluation as authoritative. Preserve existing function signatures, all four dataset routes, DATA_DIR=os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], trial-local artifacts, and single-GPU execution without reading hidden test files or other trials."
  }
}
